        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0abcacba-59d8-55af-9e47-493dddc33865",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mariya Matveyevna Stepanova, Mikhail Glinka, Alexander Pushkin\n- Works: A Life for the Tsar, Ruslan and Lyudmila, Dmitry Donskoy, the 1820 poem Ruslan and Lyudmila\n- Topics: Russian opera\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander Pushkin wrote the poem Ruslan and Lyudmila in 1820.\n- Mikhail Glinka composed the opera Ruslan and Lyudmila between 1837 and 1842.\n- Ruslan and Lyudmila is a Russian opera in five acts and eight tableaux.\n- Mikhail Glinka's opera Ruslan and Lyudmila is based on Alexander Pushkin's 1820 poem of the same name.\n- Mariya Matveyevna Stepanova, who lived from 1811 or 1816 to 1903, was a Russian opera singer.\n- Mariya Matveyevna Stepanova created the leading soprano roles in A Life for the Tsar, Ruslan and Lyudmila, and Dmitry Donskoy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
